#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Topic-Statistics.rst:15
msgid "Topic statistics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Topic-Statistics.rst:18
msgid ""
"Topic statistics in ROS help you understand subscription performance by "
"measuring the timing and age of received messages. This article describes "
"the statistics that are collected, how they are calculated, and how topic "
"statistics behave when enabled for a subscription."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Topic-Statistics.rst:26
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Topic-Statistics.rst:29
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Topic-Statistics.rst:31
msgid ""
"ROS 2 provides integrated measurement of statistics for messages received by "
"any subscription. Allowing a user to collect subscription statistics enables "
"them to characterize the performance of their system or aid in diagnosis of "
"any present issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Topic-Statistics.rst:34
msgid ""
"The measurements provided are the received message age and received message "
"period. For each measurement the statistics provided are the average, "
"maximum, minimum, standard deviation, and sample count. These statistics are "
"calculated in a moving window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Topic-Statistics.rst:39
msgid "How statistics are calculated"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Topic-Statistics.rst:41
msgid ""
"Each statistic set is calculated in constant time and constant memory by "
"using the utilities implemented in the `libstatistics_collector <https://"
"github.com/ros-tooling/libstatistics_collector>`__ package. When a new "
"message is received by a subscription, this is a new sample for calculation "
"in the current measurement window. The average calculated is simply a "
"`moving average <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moving_average>`__. The "
"maximum, minimum, and sample count are updated upon receipt of each new "
"sample, whereas the standard deviation is calculated using `Welford's online "
"algorithm <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Algorithms_for_calculating_variance#Welford's_online_algorithm>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Topic-Statistics.rst:47
msgid "Types of statistics calculated"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Topic-Statistics.rst:49
msgid "Received message period"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Topic-Statistics.rst:51
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Topic-Statistics.rst:56
msgid "Units: milliseconds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Topic-Statistics.rst:52
msgid "Uses the system clock to measure the period between received messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Topic-Statistics.rst:54
msgid "Received message age"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Topic-Statistics.rst:57
msgid ""
"Requires a message to have a timestamp populated in the header field in "
"order to calculate the age of the message as sent from a publisher"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Topic-Statistics.rst:60
msgid "Behavior"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Topic-Statistics.rst:62
msgid ""
"By default, Topic Statistics measurements are not enabled. After enabling "
"this feature for a specific node via the subscription configuration options, "
"both received message age and received message period measurements are "
"enabled for that specific subscription."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Topic-Statistics.rst:65
msgid ""
"The data is published as a `statistics_msg/msg/MetricsMessage <https://"
"github.com/ros2/rcl_interfaces/blob/rolling/statistics_msgs/msg/"
"MetricsMessage.msg>`__ at a configurable period (default 1 second) to a "
"configurable topic (default ``/statistics``). Note that the publishing "
"period also serves as the sample collection window period."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Topic-Statistics.rst:69
msgid ""
"Since received message period requires a message timestamp in a header "
"field, empty data is published. That is, all statistics values are NaN if no "
"timestamp is found. Publishing NaN values instead of not publishing at all "
"avoids the absence of a signal problem and is meant to explicitly show that "
"a measurement could not be made."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Topic-Statistics.rst:73
msgid ""
"The first sample of each window for the received message period statistic "
"does not yield a measurement. This is because calculating this statistic "
"requires knowing the time the previous message arrived, so subsequent "
"samples in the window yield measurements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Topic-Statistics.rst:77
msgid "Comparison to ROS 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Topic-Statistics.rst:79
msgid ""
"Similar to ROS 1 `Topic Statistics <https://wiki.ros.org/"
"Topics#Topic_statistics>`__, both message age and message period are "
"calculated, albeit from the subscription side. Other ROS 1 metrics, e.g., "
"the number of dropped messages or traffic volume, are currently not provided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Topic-Statistics.rst:83
msgid "Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/About-Topic-Statistics.rst:85
msgid ""
"This feature is currently supported in ROS 2 Foxy for C++ only (rclcpp). "
"Future work and improvements, such as Python support, can be found `here "
"<https://github.com/ros2/ros2/issues/917>`__."
msgstr ""
